                "reply_count": 4,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "The U.S. continues to lead in health care; however, we continue to face a crisis of high costs, quality of care, and how we reimburse our health system. \n\nThe Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Innovation was created as a solution to address these problems. But according to recent CBO reports, CMMI's initiatives have increased by $5.4 billion in direct federal spending from 2011 to 2020. \n\nThis is contrary to initial projections of generating nearly $3 billion in savings. \n\nDuring today's @housecommerce Health Subcommittee hearing, I questioned our witness on CMMI's payment models and whether they are improving patient outcomes and reducing costs.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1718303451,
                "view_count": 776
